    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-ceiling matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (72.04) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63). **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premium play, benefiting from a 14% platoon edge against Freddy Peralta and the structural advantage of a high-scoring lineup spot. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** occupies the top spot on our board for efficiency; his matchup against a high-ERA arm in Cody Bradford, combined with a 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a favorable park, makes him an elite start. **Jackson Merrill** (69.72) also earns a strong recommendation, as his 13% platoon edge against Tanner Bibee positions him to anchor our outfield productivity.\n\nWhile the core is set, we are keeping a close eye on the bench, where **Heliot Ramos** (44.02) was the final exclusion. Despite a solid projection, **Heliot Ramos** fell just short of the threshold because the optimizer favored the higher-floor efficiency of our active utility hitters against their respective right-handed matchups. Our most notable risk today remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players; specifically, **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** face pitchers like Michael Soroka and Freddy Peralta, respectively, where any last-minute shift down the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their projected fantasy output. Managers should also note that while **Luis Robert Jr.** (54.05) and **Kyle Tucker** (51.57) provide essential speed, their scores are tempered by unfavorable platoon splits; however, their ability to exploit the slow delivery of their opponents keeps them in the starting lineup given the premium we place on the stolen base category.",
